<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The shell's copy: onboarding, settings, search, the library, quick log.

  One file per area so two people can work at once; this is the "shell" area —
  everything a user reads on the way in or on the way to a setting. See
  docs/localization.md for the pipeline and docs/porting-conventions.md for the
  copy rules.

  What is deliberately *not* here, and stays a literal in Kotlin:
    - substance names, aliases, brand names, route identifiers and every
      `.wireValue` / `.name` read — those are data, and the catalog has its own
      localized names;
    - the tour mocks' substance lists and their fixed "9:41" status bar, which
      are a picture of a screenshot rather than copy;
    - "Not medical advice." — English in the Chinese build too, on purpose: it is
      the sentence that has to be legible to someone who cannot read the rest.

  Placeholders are positional (%1$s / %1$d) because Chinese reorders arguments.
-->
