    <!--
      ==================== Substance detail: binding vocabulary ====================

      `BindingAction` and `BindingAffinity` live in `:core:model`, which is a plain
      JVM module and cannot hold a resource id — so the detail screen was printing
      `.wireValue` and `.name.lowercase()` straight onto the page ("reuptakeInhibitor
      · significant"). These are the reader-facing labels for those two.

      Route, category, and the combination row's three tiers are **not** here:
      `glass.kagerou.piru.ui.labels.CoreLabels` owns those, and every screen that
      prints one goes through it — the detail screen and quick log included.

      These stayed in this file rather than moving to `strings_core_vocabulary.xml`
      on purpose. `zh_from_xcstrings.py` regenerates a whole file by looking each
      English value up in upstream's catalogue, and of these fourteen four have no
      upstream entry at all — upstream abbreviates two of them ("PAM"/"NAM"), and
      the three affinity tiers it never labels, because it draws them as dots — so
      a move would blank reviewed translations. A fifth, "significant", would come
      back re-translated: upstream has an unrelated "significant" and the script's
      last-resort case-insensitive probe finds it. `CoreLabels.bindingAction` and
      `CoreLabels.bindingAffinity` are the only readers.
    -->

